%% coins_boot.glp --- the currency on two smartphones (SGSG paper, Section 7):
%% under the boot harness, one isolate per person, each with its own key pair,
%% running the social graph of graph/core as its super-app and hosting
%% Currencies' mini-app (programs/currencies/coins/currency).  Each person trusts the
%% bundled compiler's key, reads the certified artefact currency.glpw from
%% graph/core with load_file/2 and installs it, giving the super-app one end of
%% a channel of the mediator's cards and the person's answers; alice cold-calls
%% bob, they befriend across the isolates, alice invites bob to the currency,
%% bob consents, and the handshake opens a root channel of the currency's own
%% protocol between their two executions, each activated by run/3.  Each person
%% then mints 2 and alice swaps her 2 for bob's 2, bob accepting --- the
%% currency's own swap, over the conversation the social graph delivered
%% between two smartphones.  The program is graph/core, named as :boot's second
%% argument:
%%   :artefact programs/currencies/coins/currency programs/social/graph/core
%%   :boot programs/social/coins_boot.glp programs/social/graph/core
%% Expected on the persons' screens: [alice] opened(bob), [alice] minted(2),
%% [bob] opened(alice), [bob] minted(2), [alice] swap_done(bob),
%% [bob] swap_done(alice), and the holdings each side of the swap.

procedure boot.
boot :-
    agent(ch(_?, _), ch(_?, _))@alice,
    say(alice, coins_invite, [bob], ch(_?, _))@alice,
    agent(ch(_?, _), ch(_?, _))@bob,
    say(bob, coins_consent, [alice], ch(_?, _))@bob.

%% Every agent's initial goal is agent(ch(_?,_),ch(_?,_)), the person channel
%% first and the network channel second (GLP-Spec maglp.tex, Definition
%% "Multiagent GLP"), which the program, graph/core, answers: a boot defines
%% no agent/2, and the person goal's first act names the entry the program
%% starts (IGLP 0e1c9e0, Implementation Notes, "Boot").  The person scripted
%% at each agent, say/4, run on its person channel in the person's place,
%% tells the agent the entry, sg_init/4, with its own key, its mode and the
%% keys of the peers it knows, its ground arguments, alice and bob being the
%% atoms that stand for the keys in a simulation ("An agent learns the keys of
%% its peers from its person"; Remark "Agent Names"), and reads nothing.
SayAct ::= sg_init(Key, Constant, List(Key)).
SayIn  ::= [SayAct | SayEnd].
SayEnd ::= [].

exported procedure say(Key?, Constant?, List(Key)?, Channel(Stream(Constant), SayIn)?).
say(P, M, Qs, ch(_, [sg_init(P?, M?, Qs?)])).
